WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.906 --> 00:00:06.823
[leather scraping]

00:00:10.580 --> 00:00:14.430
My name is Thomas Rago, and I am co-owner

00:00:14.430 --> 00:00:17.700
of Rago Brothers Shoe &amp; Leather Repair.

00:00:17.700 --> 00:00:20.282
Our team is now going to walk you through

00:00:20.282 --> 00:00:24.910
the restoration and repair
of a Hermès Birkin bag

00:00:24.910 --> 00:00:28.120
that's valued in excess of $10,000.

00:00:28.120 --> 00:00:30.650
We received the bag, and
immediately we realized

00:00:30.650 --> 00:00:32.790
the bag needs new tubing in the handles.

00:00:32.790 --> 00:00:34.530
The corners are worn,

00:00:34.530 --> 00:00:36.413
it needs new feet,

00:00:36.413 --> 00:00:38.538
and it needs color restoration.

00:00:39.961 --> 00:00:42.711
[seams ripping]

00:00:44.040 --> 00:00:47.660
First off, we're now going
to give this bag to Luis.

00:00:47.660 --> 00:00:52.290
He's going to begin the process
of deconstructing the bag.

00:00:54.530 --> 00:00:57.620
We do that by opening up the bag,

00:00:57.620 --> 00:00:59.943
pulling the binding out
of the inside of the bag,

00:00:59.943 --> 00:01:02.380
pulling the stitches
out one stitch at a time

00:01:02.380 --> 00:01:05.741
so that we don't damage
existing stitch holes.

00:01:09.910 --> 00:01:12.020
Using a very sharp razor knife,

00:01:12.020 --> 00:01:15.190
we need to take all four
sides of the bag off

00:01:15.190 --> 00:01:18.625
to access the piping on
the bottom of the bag.

00:01:24.410 --> 00:01:26.430
We've got the bag apart now,

00:01:26.430 --> 00:01:27.940
but we need to get the excess glue

00:01:27.940 --> 00:01:28.868
and all the stitching out.

00:01:28.868 --> 00:01:31.230
So we are going to take a piece of rubber

00:01:31.230 --> 00:01:34.410
and we're going to rub
off that excess glue

00:01:34.410 --> 00:01:36.600
and pull out the old stitches,

00:01:36.600 --> 00:01:40.091
so that when we reglue this bag, it holds.

00:01:42.130 --> 00:01:43.970
Upon taking off the old feet,

00:01:43.970 --> 00:01:47.370
we see that we need to
make the holes larger

00:01:47.370 --> 00:01:49.050
to fit the new feet.

00:01:49.050 --> 00:01:50.858
So what we're going to need to do

00:01:50.858 --> 00:01:53.349
is take a punch, and punch that hole

00:01:53.349 --> 00:01:55.699
slightly bigger than it is now.

00:02:07.770 --> 00:02:10.670
The tubing inside of
those handles are plastic.

00:02:10.670 --> 00:02:12.230
The person may have weighted it.

00:02:12.230 --> 00:02:15.630
So, over time, plastic
breaks down. It broke.

00:02:15.630 --> 00:02:18.005
We need to replace that tubing

00:02:18.005 --> 00:02:21.479
on the inside of the handles.

00:02:21.479 --> 00:02:23.990
The only way that we're
going to access that tubing

00:02:23.990 --> 00:02:25.930
is to take the handle apart.

00:02:25.930 --> 00:02:28.450
So very carefully, with a knife,

00:02:28.450 --> 00:02:32.761
we need to take out
each stitch one by one.

00:02:38.060 --> 00:02:41.170
So, now we have the tubing out.

00:02:41.170 --> 00:02:43.747
We cut and measure the new tubing,

00:02:44.720 --> 00:02:49.078
and we need to lay it
on the existing handle,

00:02:49.078 --> 00:02:50.803
close it,

00:02:50.803 --> 00:02:53.990
and then we need to restitch that tubing

00:02:53.990 --> 00:02:54.964
back into the handle.

00:02:54.964 --> 00:02:59.386
And that's done one
stitch at a time by hand.

00:03:08.210 --> 00:03:10.673
The piping leather is damaged.

00:03:10.673 --> 00:03:12.393
It needs to be replaced.

00:03:12.393 --> 00:03:16.130
Fortunately, we have
leather that is the same

00:03:16.130 --> 00:03:18.430
as the leather that came off of the bag,

00:03:18.430 --> 00:03:20.038
but it's too thick.

00:03:28.810 --> 00:03:29.992
We have a skiving machine,

00:03:29.992 --> 00:03:32.775
a machine that splits that leather,

00:03:32.775 --> 00:03:34.483
makes it thinner.

00:03:38.260 --> 00:03:41.000
But even so, after we thin it,

00:03:41.000 --> 00:03:43.060
we have to take a razor-sharp knife

00:03:43.060 --> 00:03:45.050
and even make it thinner.

00:03:56.290 --> 00:03:59.358
After we take the now very thin leather

00:03:59.358 --> 00:04:02.680
and wrap it around the new plastic piping,

00:04:02.680 --> 00:04:05.586
we need to clamp the edges to close it.

00:04:07.648 --> 00:04:11.940
[sewing machine stitching]

00:04:11.940 --> 00:04:16.500
Hermès bags are made one
at a time and by hand.

00:04:16.500 --> 00:04:19.090
So we are going to have
to take a lot of time

00:04:19.090 --> 00:04:22.540
to bring this bag back to
the condition it was in

00:04:22.540 --> 00:04:24.340
when it was first bought.

00:04:25.460 --> 00:04:26.720
The bag is inside out.

00:04:26.720 --> 00:04:29.330
We can see the same stitch holes.

00:04:29.330 --> 00:04:30.520
First thing we're going to do

00:04:30.520 --> 00:04:33.446
is we're going to stitch the two sides.

00:04:36.140 --> 00:04:40.390
After we do the two sides,
we're going to sew the top.

00:04:44.770 --> 00:04:46.320
And then, finally,

00:04:46.320 --> 00:04:48.610
we are going to sew around the bottom

00:04:48.610 --> 00:04:50.800
where we put the new piping in.

00:04:55.708 --> 00:04:57.418
Now that we have the structure of the bag

00:04:57.418 --> 00:04:58.818
back to where it was,

00:04:58.818 --> 00:05:00.643
we have to think about cleaning

00:05:00.643 --> 00:05:02.840
and conditioning and recoloring this bag.

00:05:02.840 --> 00:05:03.673
It's faded.

00:05:03.673 --> 00:05:05.423
The color is just not there.

00:05:06.850 --> 00:05:09.120
Before we can redye this bag,

00:05:09.120 --> 00:05:12.530
we have to make sure that
all the surface dirt is off.

00:05:12.530 --> 00:05:15.300
If there is any polish
or conditioner on it,

00:05:15.300 --> 00:05:16.290
we need to take that off

00:05:16.290 --> 00:05:20.248
so that when we put the dye
on this bag, it adheres.

00:05:23.500 --> 00:05:25.310
We are using a cleaning solution,

00:05:25.310 --> 00:05:29.735
and we take a very soft finger brush

00:05:29.735 --> 00:05:31.351
and we scrub the bag

00:05:31.351 --> 00:05:34.182
to remove all the excess dirt and film

00:05:34.182 --> 00:05:36.870
and polish that we need to get off.

00:05:36.870 --> 00:05:38.080
After we clean it,

00:05:38.080 --> 00:05:41.502
we're going to take a clean
cloth and wipe it off.

00:05:45.986 --> 00:05:50.450
What we need to do now is
we need to match the color.

00:05:50.450 --> 00:05:52.600
We'll look on the bag
and we'll look for a spot

00:05:52.600 --> 00:05:56.470
that really looks like the bag
did look like 10 years ago.

00:05:56.470 --> 00:05:59.720
And then we will mix
color, water-based paint,

00:05:59.720 --> 00:06:02.740
to match that part of the bag.

00:06:02.740 --> 00:06:06.300
The mixing of the dye is all done by eye

00:06:06.300 --> 00:06:07.790
under the correct lighting.

00:06:07.790 --> 00:06:09.073
Depending on the color,

00:06:09.073 --> 00:06:10.920
the guy may have to mix the dyes

00:06:10.920 --> 00:06:13.640
three or four times before he's satisfied

00:06:13.640 --> 00:06:16.320
that he got close to the original color.

00:06:21.220 --> 00:06:23.270
Depending on the texture of the bag,

00:06:23.270 --> 00:06:26.260
that will determine what
applicator we will use

00:06:26.260 --> 00:06:28.491
to put the dye on the bag.

00:06:36.790 --> 00:06:38.850
Now that we have the dye on the bag,

00:06:38.850 --> 00:06:40.720
there are some finishing
touches we need to do

00:06:40.720 --> 00:06:42.570
that really makes the job.

00:06:42.570 --> 00:06:44.180
We need to re-edge the handles,

00:06:44.180 --> 00:06:46.860
and we need to re-edge the top of the bag.

00:06:46.860 --> 00:06:49.350
Now, the edging on the handle
and the top of the bag,

00:06:49.350 --> 00:06:51.260
not the same color as the bag.

00:06:51.260 --> 00:06:54.740
So we have to go back
again to mix the color

00:06:54.740 --> 00:06:58.510
to match the original
edging that was on the bag.

00:07:10.250 --> 00:07:11.600
The dye is dried.

00:07:11.600 --> 00:07:13.040
We need to condition the bag.

00:07:13.040 --> 00:07:14.850
And the reason why we're conditioning it

00:07:14.850 --> 00:07:16.760
is to hold that dye.

00:07:16.760 --> 00:07:19.910
That, along with resealing the bag,

00:07:19.910 --> 00:07:20.743
is going to make certain

00:07:20.743 --> 00:07:24.443
that this bag stays looking
good for years to come.

00:07:29.020 --> 00:07:32.347
Myself, my team, we're really proud

00:07:32.347 --> 00:07:34.013
of the way this bag came out,

00:07:34.013 --> 00:07:35.271
and we only wish that we could see

00:07:35.271 --> 00:07:38.160
the expression on the client's face

00:07:38.160 --> 00:07:41.341
when she opens up the bag and looks at it.

00:07:41.341 --> 00:07:44.648
It really is a rewarding process.

